{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_15-11-32-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nkn={\\\"id\\\":\\\"a92a355fb0ca4aa7a0b62580ea79f7fa-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n \\\"statement\\\":\\\"In handlePrepareReply a reply whose Ballot differs from lb.lastTriedBallot increments lb.nacks and returns before the reply is appended to lb.prepareReplies, and no repair is attempted on that path; the sub-case dispatch is guarded by len(lb.prepareReplies) >= SlowQuorumSize(), so a recovery whose answers are all rejections keeps only its own self reply, selects no sub-case and emits no PreAccept, Accept or Commit for that attempt. The makeBallot-plus-prepare restarts that do exist live in the two proposal-phase handlers (handlePreAcceptReply and handleAcceptReply) when a majority of replies reports a higher ballot, and each of those is executed only while r.IsLeader is true.\\\",\n \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Recovery where the replicas that answer the Prepare have a stored bal above the recovering replica's fixed tried ballot, so every answer is a rejection rather than a matching-ballot reply (epaxos/epaxos.go:1204-1222, with epaxos/epaxos.go:439-451, 855-868 and 1016-1033).\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-decl-prepare-reply\\\",\\\"s-makeballot\\\",\\\"s-preaccept-reply\\\",\\\"s-nack-accept\\\",\\\"s-isleader-default\\\",\\\"s-betheleader\\\"],\n \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"911d45335b3047178a6fd739f24b2cfb\\\":[17,18,19,20,23,24,25,28,29,30,31],\\\"c68b6de1442e45ffa00ddaf4df9b32e6\\\":[12,17],\\\"c342db60ffff4e42889bf53646049491\\\":[12,17]},\n \\\"changed_premise\\\":\\\"Corrected where the IsLeader-gated repair lives: the prepare-recovery rejection path contains no repair at all (it only counts nacks and returns), while the makeBallot-plus-bcastPrepare restarts are in handlePreAcceptReply and handleAcceptReply. The conclusion (a fully rejected recovery attempt stays inert with no enabled repair for a non-designated replica) is unchanged; the earlier wording attributed the gated repair to handlePrepareReply.\\\",\n \\\"affected_uses\\\":[\\\"0a3fee9ceb2441d89d6954ef50be3429-interpretation-0\\\"]}\nrec=json.load(open('draft/update21.json'))['interpretations'][0]\nrec['rationale']=rec['rationale'].replace(\n \\\"No repair exists inside the snapshot for the blocked case: makeBallot's climb and the nack path's recovery are both gated on IsLeader, so the blocked replica's attempts stay inert until the master designates it (epaxos/epaxos.go:439-451, 1216-1235, 1121-1125).\\\",\n \\\"No repair exists inside the snapshot for the blocked case, and the prepare-recovery path has none of its own: handlePrepareReply counts the rejection and returns (epaxos/epaxos.go:1216-1219), the makeBallot-plus-prepare restarts that do exist sit in the proposal-phase handlers and are gated on r.IsLeader (epaxos/epaxos.go:855-868 and 1016-1033), and makeBallot's climb above maxRecvBallot is likewise gated on it (epaxos/epaxos.go:439-451); the blocked replica's attempts therefore stay inert until the master designates it through BeTheLeader (epaxos/epaxos.go:1121-1125).\\\")\nrec['knowledge']=[{\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"a92a355fb0ca4aa7a0b62580ea79f7fa-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":5,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"the prepare-recovery rejection has no repair; the gated restarts are on the proposal-phase handlers\\\"},\n                 {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"a92a355fb0ca4aa7a0b62580ea79f7fa-knowledge-1\\\",\\\"revision\\\":4,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"fixed ballot per replica, climbing only with IsLeader; boundary against the peers' stored ballot\\\"}]\nrec['counterevidence'].append(\\\"The conclusion does not depend on where the gated restarts sit: the prepare-recovery path has no repair (epaxos/epaxos.go:1216-1219), and the two restarts that exist belong to the proposal-phase handlers, which a blocked recoverer never reaches because its prepare never completes.\\\")\njson.dump({\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Corrected a retained claim against its source: the prepare-recovery rejection path (handlePrepareReply) contains no repair at all, while the IsLeader-gated makeBallot-plus-prepare restarts belong to the proposal-phase handlers. The behavior entry is revised under its existing id with the affected interpretation named, and the recovery-authority account is updated to cite the correct sites; the conclusion is unchanged and in fact rests on a simpler basis.\\\",\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[kn],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[rec]},open('draft/update25.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written')\nPY\ntimeout 120 /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_15-11-32-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission update25.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
